  (text "S1 KW12-3 SWITCH (off-board), J3 H17-I17\nJ3 pin 1 = NC contact -> HOME (D10 / GPIO10), pin 2 = COM -> GND. NO unused.\nNC closed at rest; firmware INPUT_PULLUP + R4 10k to 3V3.\nOpen wire reads STOP, a short to GND can read READY: test both states." (at 72.39 246.28 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid d79ceea2-a9df-5ee8-be46-a6a412b7630c)
  )
  (rectangle (start 170.18 196) (end 297.18 252)
    (stroke (width 0.254) (type default))
    (fill (type none))
    (uuid d739b133-f826-5a8e-8403-54e792533bac)
  )
  (text "A4988 CURRENT LIMIT - DECISIONS.md D30 (2026-10-21)\nVref = 0.85 V  (about 1.06 A, at the carrier's maximum).  Vref = 8 x I x Rsense, R100 = 0.100 ohm.\nSupersedes D29 / Rev D README (1.35 A, 1.08 V): 1.08 V is NOT reachable on this carrier\n(red R100 clones top out at ~0.79-0.85 V Vref on 3.3 V logic). VDD stays 3.3 V.\nSet Vref with 12 V on, motor DISCONNECTED, logic powered, EN high: black probe on driver GND,\nred on the trim pot. Read both sense resistors first. Heatsink stays on; 60 min hold test." (at 172.72 197.28 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid aac48444-0ede-5f7f-8536-f18d08dcad7f)
  )
  (text "MICROSTEP (MS1/MS2/MS3): all three tied LOW (GND) = FULL STEP -> config `microsteps` = 1\n(config/robot.example.json). If they are moved to +3V3 (1/16 step) set `microsteps` = 16 for\nthat station before the first run. Hardware and config MUST match: mismatch = wrong lengths." (at 172.72 219 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 7742d086-fc59-5d9b-b3bf-aa9fae5308d1)
  )
  (text "DO NOT RAISE VDD TO 5 V. A4988 VDD, RESET, SLEEP = 3.3 V from the XIAO 3V3 pin; the ESP32-C3\nGPIOs (STEP, DIR, EN) are not 5 V tolerant.  Pull-ups to 3.3 V only." (at 172.72 232 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid e055e16e-da55-5441-afed-309c3dfb148c)
  )
  (text "FUSING IS AT THE SUPPLY END: branch fuses F1-F4 (rating TBD) and F0 7.5 A (existing, recorded,\nnot approved) sit before the long cables. No fuse, reverse-polarity or over-voltage protection\non this board. Rev D TP0-TP4 are not parts on the perfboard: probe the module pins / holes." (at 172.72 240 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 42274879-ee34-5d5d-bdfc-ecea670f1b54)
  )
  (text "POWER-UP SEQUENCE (summary of Rev D sheet 5)" (at 304.8 17.78 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left top))
    (uuid fb726acc-dd62-54fa-b17b-016a6b65c929)
  )
  (text "1. Remove USB and 12 V; let C1 discharge; do not short it with a tool.\n2. Check the board against this netlist with a meter: both A4988 GND\n   pads to J1-2; 12V, +3V3, 5VB/5VD/+5V each free of shorts to GND.\n3. Test the supply and the buck alone; set 5.00 V at U1 OUT+ (net 5VB)\n   BEFORE connecting any load. JP1 OPEN.\n4. Add XIAO, then A4988, one at a time; power off between changes.\n5. 12 V on, EN high, motor disconnected: check +3V3 and set Vref\n   0.85 V (D30). Never guess Vref from the screw direction.\n6. Power off; connect the coil pairs (1A/1B, 2A/2B). Never plug or\n   unplug the motor with power on.\n7. Run only a short, unloaded jog and the switch test. No suspended\n   load or room operation until bench-checked." (at 304.8 22.86 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 229f2f3e-37b5-554c-8c17-4b39f185f65e)
  )
  (text "USB / EXTERNAL POWER" (at 304.8 76.2 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left top))
    (uuid f3d76ba9-3aca-5043-9e69-d95639c545eb)
  )
  (text "USB plugged in: JP1 OPEN.  Standalone from 12 V: USB unplugged,\nJP1 CLOSED.  Never USB + 12 V with JP1 closed (two sources meet\non VBUS).  Change JP1 only with all power off." (at 304.8 81.28 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 929c34ac-557a-58ce-aac8-d8b33c87a783)
  )
  (text "PERFBOARD HOLE MAP (generated, component side, A01 top-left)" (at 304.8 94 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left top))
    (uuid 56a9324e-11ed-5d8f-bb53-5915836b9c2f)
  )
  (text "J1: 1=X01  2=X03\nJ2: 1=X05  2=X06  3=X07  4=X08\nJ5: 1=C17  2=D17  3=E17  4=F17\nJ3: 1=H17  2=I17\nJP1: 1=S11  2=R11\nC1: 1=T02  2=T03\nD1: 1=T11  2=X11\nU1: 1=X15  2=W15  3=V15  4=U15  5=T15\nR1: E13 - E10\nR2: C10 - C11\nR3: D10 - D11\nR4: H13 - H16\nU2: B03..H03 (5V..D7) and B09..H09 (D0..D6)\nU3: L03..L10 (pads 9..16) and Q03..Q10 (pads 8..1)\n\nPin 1 = first hole listed.  U1 EN (T15) and XIAO D0, D6, D7,\nD8, D9 are unconnected on the board (no-connect flags)." (at 304.8 99.06 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 9372620f-a245-5311-b2dc-23ef5ca8e84d)
  )
  (text "DIFFERENCES FROM THE REV D SCHEMATIC (perfboard wins)" (at 304.8 140 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) bold) (justify left top))
    (uuid 99636d7a-613c-564b-9aed-81d1bf9ea280)
  )
  (text "Current limit: Rev D sheet 3 / README show 1.35 A, Vref 1.08 V (D29).\n  This sheet follows D30: Vref 0.85 V, about 1.06 A.\nEncoder: Rev D sheet 3 draws DIR to GND and OUT open at the encoder.\n  The board has a 4-pin J5 only (3V3, GND, SDA, SCL), so those two\n  are on the encoder board, not on the perfboard.\nTest points TP0-TP4 of Rev D are not parts on the perfboard.\nGrounds: Rev D shows one GND; the board has two A4988 GND pads (pad 7\n  motor return, pad 1 logic) tied by wire S03-O11 = one GND net here.\nPackages as built: R2/R3 stand upright (2.54 mm), R1/R4 lie (7.62 mm);\n  J1 is a 5.08 mm terminal pitch (2.54 mm header otherwise).\nNet names: perfboard 3V3 / 5V / 12V are the +3V3 / +5V / +12V power\n  symbols; 5VB = buck OUT+ / D1 anode, 5VD = D1 cathode / JP1." (at 304.8 145 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid f5a2006a-e128-587f-a477-1900e591e7c0)
  )

